; fault_access.kasm -- a misaligned load faults, in both machines.
;
; The access faults are the ones a memory-system change is most likely to
; break, and until this program existed nothing checked them on the RTL side at
; all. Deleting the misaligned check from k2g_core.sv outright left every
; testbench and the whole cosimulation passing: `kgen` chooses every address so
; it cannot fault, and the shipped programs are all well-behaved by
; construction.
;
; The emulator's own tests cover this (tests/faults_and_io.rs), which is
; precisely why it needs to be here too -- a fault the reference model raises
; and the hardware does not is invisible to a test that only asks the reference
; model.
;
; Unlike the decode faults, alignment cannot be known before execute: the
; address is a register plus a displacement. So this stays predicated like any
; other execute-time fault -- see fault_squashed.kasm.

        .org    0

        puc32   r1, 3
        ld32    r2, [r1]        ; MISALIGNED_LOAD -- 3 is not 4-byte aligned
        halt
